Usage: bun claudekit/probe/main.ts [--run] [--base-only] [--report] [--runs N] [--model M] [--alt-threshold T] [--sizes A,B] [--max-total-usd U] [--dir D]
With no --run it is a dry run: it prints the plan and the expected cost, and makes no call.
--base-only stops after the base sessions and runs no fork, which exercises the paid path and measures the base context for the price of one base.
--report reads the forks that --dir already holds in results.jsonl and reports them, free and with no call, which is how a round stopped by its cost cap is still reported.
--run makes the paid calls. N is a whole number of at least 3 (default 11, the citable floor of 10 and a spare, so a fork lost to a transient failure does not cost the round its citability), M is one of claude-sonnet-5-5, claude-haiku-5-5, claude-opus-5-5 (default claude-sonnet-5-5), T is the candidate threshold in tokens (default 100000, and the reference arm is 140000), A,B are base sizes in tokens (default 90000), and U is a cost above 0 that stops the round (default 26).
